This is an example code to generate a FCC crystal in periodic space and then shear it.

Note: the code requires to modify particle.h in the source code of mechsys:

Line 111:
  //  bool   IsFree             () {return (!vxf&&!vyf&&!vzf&&!wxf&&!wyf&&!wzf)||FixFree;};                       ///< Ask if the particle has any constrain in its movement
    bool   IsFree             () {return (!vxf&&!vyf&&!vzf)||FixFree;};                       ///< Ask if the particle has any constrain in its movement

so that fixed-rotation are still considered free particles for cross-boundary contact detection
